    "result_text": "BUILD SUCCESS \u2014 `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`.\n\nThe redesign is complete and the suite is green. Here's what I changed:\n\n## New owner identity\n\n`customerCode` is now `<REGION>-<HASH8>` (e.g. `NSW-16E6609E`), with sequence numbers dropped entirely.\n\n**New utilities** (in `util/`, alongside the other pure derived-value helpers):\n- **`Sha256`** \u2014 shared SHA-256 hex helper: `hex(v)` (full lower-case) and `prefix(v, n)` (first *n* upper-case hex chars). Extracted so the hashing lives in one place.\n- **`CustomerCode`** \u2014 encapsulates the identity format: `of(region, normalizedTelephone, lastName)` builds `<REGION>-<HASH8>` (HASH8 = first 8 upper-case hex of SHA-256 over `telephone + lastName`), and `regionOf(code)` reads the REGION back out.\n\n**Changed logic:**\n- **`AssignCustomerCode`** \u2014 rewritten. Region comes from `Locality.of(city, postcode)` (postcode-preferred), hash from the owner's already-E.164-normalized telephone + last name. No longer depends on `OwnerRepository`, so the per-city count/sequence is gone.\n- **`OwnerMapper.locality`** \u2014 now the REGION portion of the customerCode (`CustomerCode.regionOf`), falling back to `Locality.of` only for owners without a code yet. This \"moves the locality derivation onto the new identity\" as the spec requires.\n- **`HouseholdNormalizer`** \u2014 its private `sha256hex` was deleted; it now reuses `Sha256.prefix`, eliminating the duplicate hashing code.\n\n**Automatically inherited the new identity** (they already read `customerCode`, no logic change needed):\n- `membershipNumber` (`<customerCode>-M<YY>`) in `OwnerMapper`\n- `checkDigit` (Luhn over the code's digits) via `CheckDigit`\n- the create audit record in `AuditOwnerCreated`\n\nI also updated stale javadoc/examples in `OwnerMapper` and `EnsureCityCapacity` that referenced the old `CITY3-LAST3-NNNN` sequence scheme.",
